{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:StochasticMechanics.MarkovClosureMapAxiomatic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"StochasticMechanics.MarkovClosureMapAxiomatic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BraidLinkTypes"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.track_C_c_3_eq_neg_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.track_C_c_3_eq_neg_two","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/markov-closure-map-axiomatic.lean#L85-L91","doc":"**Track C c_3 = -2 derived from `TrackCReducedAxiom`.** Under the\naxiomatic Markov-closure-map class + Track-C reduced axiom, the\nHopf-Jones identification c_3 = -2 follows immediately. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TrackCReducedAxiom.c_3_eq_jones_hopf_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrackCReducedAxiom.c_3_eq_jones_hopf_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/markov-closure-map-axiomatic.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The c_3 coefficient in the τ_M expansion factors as the Hopf-link\nJones at q=1, scaled by the Hoefsmit b³ substrate factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TrackCReducedAxiom.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrackCReducedAxiom.mk","kind":"ctor","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/markov-closure-map-axiomatic.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TrackCReducedAxiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrackCReducedAxiom","kind":"class","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/markov-closure-map-axiomatic.lean#L69-L79","doc":"**Track C reduced axiom**: the dominant 3-fold Markov-closure\nsub-braid contribution at order ε^6 factors through the\n`closure 2`-typed Hopf-link Jones at q=1.\n\nThis axiomatises the substantive combinatorial content that\nearlier lived in `ThreeFoldMarkovHopfExtraction`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovClosureMap2Strand.jones_hopf_at_one_eq_neg_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovClosureMap2Strand.jones_hopf_at_one_eq_neg_two","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/markov-closure-map-axiomatic.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The classical Hopf-Jones value: J_Hopf(1) = -2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovClosureMap2Strand.jones_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovClosureMap2Strand.jones_at_one","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/markov-closure-map-axiomatic.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Jones polynomial of the closure at q=1, for any k. For k=2 this\ngives J_Hopf(1) = -2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovClosureMap2Strand.is_hopf_at_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovClosureMap2Strand.is_hopf_at_two","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/markov-closure-map-axiomatic.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The Hopf link is the specific case k = 2 (value equality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovClosureMap2Strand.closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovClosureMap2Strand.closure","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/markov-closure-map-axiomatic.lean#L53-L53","doc":"The link-valued closure of σ_1^k in B_2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovClosureMap2Strand.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovClosureMap2Strand.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/markov-closure-map-axiomatic.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovClosureMap2Strand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovClosureMap2Strand","kind":"class","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/markov-closure-map-axiomatic.lean#L40-L60","doc":"**Abstract Markov-closure map** for 2-strand braids of length k.\nEncodes the categorical statement:\n`Markov-closure(σ_1^k in B_2) = T(2, k) (torus link)`.\n\nThe specific case `k = 2 ⇒ Hopf link` is the axiomatic input\nused for the c_3 = -2 derivation.\n\nUses **value-level equalities** on `Link` (the inductive type\nfrom `braid-link-types.lean`) rather than type-level equalities,\navoiding transport issues that arise with `... = Unit`-style\ntype identifications. ","signatureChunk":0}]}